WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.742 --> 00:00:03.418
- Today we're going to be learning about earthships,

00:00:03.418 --> 00:00:05.866
and I'm so excited to be here.

00:00:05.866 --> 00:00:07.269
I'm gonna be living in an earthship,

00:00:07.269 --> 00:00:10.218
which is a sustainable home, for 24 hours,

00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:11.528
and learning what it really means

00:00:11.528 --> 00:00:13.752
to live 100 percent off the grid.

00:00:13.752 --> 00:00:17.085
(dramatic violin music)

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.017
- Here we are at (mumbles) Earthship,

00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:29.490
the place where you'll be staying tonight.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.602
Let's go check it out.

00:00:30.602 --> 00:00:33.162
We'll start back here at the master bedroom.

00:00:33.162 --> 00:00:34.556
- This room looks so comfortable.

00:00:34.556 --> 00:00:36.290
I'm so excited to stay in it.

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.639
- [Lauren] Yeah, and Mike Reynolds really wanted

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:38.959
to showcase that you can have all

00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:41.602
of the creature comforts that you would normally have,

00:00:41.602 --> 00:00:43.828
just living off grid and sustainably.

00:00:43.828 --> 00:00:45.818
All of our appliances and lights

00:00:45.818 --> 00:00:48.151
are powered by solar panels.

00:00:48.504 --> 00:00:51.554
When rain falls, it comes and lands on our roof,

00:00:51.554 --> 00:00:54.352
and then it travels down this path,

00:00:54.352 --> 00:00:56.612
and goes into this salad bowl,

00:00:56.612 --> 00:00:59.121
and it collects in the cistern.

00:00:59.121 --> 00:01:01.517
- [Auri] And then that is used for the house?

00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:03.022
- [Lauren] Yes, exactly.

00:01:03.022 --> 00:01:04.638
We're gonna cool down your space for you.

00:01:04.638 --> 00:01:05.471
- [Auri] Cool.

00:01:05.471 --> 00:01:07.642
- So we start by opening up this door,

00:01:07.642 --> 00:01:09.708
and that has a vent tube that goes

00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:11.579
all the way to the back of the building

00:01:11.579 --> 00:01:13.320
and is buried in the berm.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:14.153
- Cool.

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:16.133
- Then, from there, we're gonna open up

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.656
your transom windows, which are above the doors,

00:01:18.656 --> 00:01:20.783
those have already been opened for you.

00:01:20.783 --> 00:01:21.616
- Nice.

00:01:21.616 --> 00:01:24.783
- And then, we open up the vent boxes.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.990
- Oh cool! I can feel the breeze.

00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:30.228
It just smells so good in here.

00:01:30.228 --> 00:01:32.976
I just smell all the herbs, and I know

00:01:32.976 --> 00:01:34.598
the air is so fresh, because there's all

00:01:34.598 --> 00:01:37.348
these plants here. Mmm, rosemary.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:44.610
Okay, I'm cold, so I'm gonna try to close this vent here.

00:01:57.464 --> 00:01:58.714
- Oh, I got it!

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:01.870
Yay, I got it.

00:02:02.564 --> 00:02:03.397
I'm gonna go meet the guy

00:02:03.397 --> 00:02:06.220
who designed and built these structures.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.803
- Humanity has six basic needs,

00:02:09.432 --> 00:02:12.327
that you can't discount any of them.

00:02:12.327 --> 00:02:14.871
It's comfortable shelter, we all need it.

00:02:14.871 --> 00:02:17.830
We all need water, we all need electricity.

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:20.312
We all need to do something with our sewage.

00:02:20.312 --> 00:02:21.978
We all need to so something with our garbage,

00:02:21.978 --> 00:02:23.569
and we all need food.

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:25.650
This vessel, that we call the earthship,

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.443
provides these things via encounter

00:02:28.443 --> 00:02:31.860
of Earth phenomena, like sun, rain, wind,

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.553
to provide sustenance for the person who's in it.

00:02:35.553 --> 00:02:38.103
It's all free; it's all here already.

00:02:38.103 --> 00:02:40.662
If you have sustenance, then money

00:02:40.662 --> 00:02:43.579
becomes paper, which is what it is.

00:02:44.171 --> 00:02:45.618
- I'm gonna pick some of these tomatoes

00:02:45.618 --> 00:02:49.785
for dinner, with some rice and all that I brought.

00:02:50.452 --> 00:02:54.152
This is my dinner that I made with the tomatoes.

00:02:54.152 --> 00:02:55.485
I'm excited to eat.

00:02:55.485 --> 00:02:59.184
I just feel so good in a space that I know is not

00:02:59.184 --> 00:03:02.600
exploiting the environment, but trying to work with it.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.456
You see all these lights? You see all these lights here?

00:03:05.456 --> 00:03:09.001
They came from the sun; the power came from the sun.

00:03:09.001 --> 00:03:12.043
I'm brushing my teeth with rain water.

00:03:12.043 --> 00:03:14.793
I went pee, and now I'm flushing,

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:17.532
and it's gonna go feed the plants.

00:03:17.532 --> 00:03:20.357
I'm taking a hot shower powered by the sun

00:03:20.357 --> 00:03:21.515
(Laughs)

00:03:21.515 --> 00:03:24.198
(mellow chimes play)

00:03:24.198 --> 00:03:27.238
Wow, what a beautiful way to wake up.

00:03:27.238 --> 00:03:29.355
So, I've decided I want an earthship,

00:03:29.355 --> 00:03:31.113
and I want to build one. What should I do?

00:03:31.113 --> 00:03:32.498
- [Lauren] Well we have classes that teach you

00:03:32.498 --> 00:03:33.824
how to build your own earthship,

00:03:33.824 --> 00:03:35.762
and they're about four weeks long,

00:03:35.762 --> 00:03:38.550
and we get students from all over the world,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.778
and right here we have Mike Reynolds

00:03:40.778 --> 00:03:44.926
teaching students on the job how to build an earthship.

00:03:44.926 --> 00:03:46.880
- So, what are all these bottles for?

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.471
- So, we build all of our buildings

00:03:48.471 --> 00:03:50.944
with recycled materials, and these bottles

00:03:50.944 --> 00:03:55.194
are given to us from the dump, or recycling center.

00:03:55.199 --> 00:03:57.166
- [Auri] And you also build with tires?

00:03:57.166 --> 00:03:58.716
- [Lauren] Yup, tires are the main

00:03:58.716 --> 00:03:59.707
structure for the building.

00:03:59.707 --> 00:04:00.863
- And why is that?

00:04:00.863 --> 00:04:02.671
- [Lauren] We have lots of used tires

00:04:02.671 --> 00:04:04.644
that are just discarded and

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.811
they support the building really well.

00:04:10.135 --> 00:04:12.335
- [Mike] Our relationship of humanity to Earth,

00:04:12.335 --> 00:04:15.595
if we're not contributing to this relationship,

00:04:15.595 --> 00:04:18.012
if we're only taking from it,

00:04:18.112 --> 00:04:20.398
it's just eventually not gonna work anymore,

00:04:20.398 --> 00:04:23.892
and it's starting to not work for the humans.

00:04:23.892 --> 00:04:26.161
The earth will be fine, the earth will just get

00:04:26.161 --> 00:04:29.545
so it can't support humans, and humans will be extinct.

00:04:29.545 --> 00:04:31.788
Our dance with this planet is about over.

00:04:31.788 --> 00:04:33.673
If we dance in a different way,

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.325
if we dance with it, rather than just

00:04:35.325 --> 00:04:39.158
taking from it, then we can last a lot longer.

00:04:39.609 --> 00:04:42.942
(dramatic violin music)

00:04:50.106 --> 00:04:52.484
- [Auri] Bye, beautiful earthship. I'll miss you.

